# Section 25 – Query Cost Modeling and Execution Plan Optimization

## Overview
Explored the mathematical formulas PostgreSQL uses to estimate query execution costs and evaluate when index scans outperform sequential reads.

## Topics Covered
- Foundations of PostgreSQL Query Cost Units and Planner Math
- Manually Computing Execution Costs Using Page and Tuple Constants
- Refining Cost Formulas Across Different Scan Operations
- Distinguishing Startup Costs from Total Execution Costs
- Understanding Hierarchical Cost Propagation in Execution Trees
- Evaluating Planner Index Selection vs. Sequential Scan Thresholds

## Technology
- PostgreSQL
- SQL

## Learning Outcome
Developed the ability to calculate query planner cost estimates manually, interpret hierarchical execution trees, and optimize index utilization in PostgreSQL.
